# The other examples rely on the repository's root .gitignore, which already
# covers .horus/ and target/. This one needs a file of its own because a C++
# build also drops a `compile_commands.json` symlink in the project root
# (run_cpp links it there for clangd) and the root .gitignore does not mention
# it — so `horus build` here would otherwise leave the working tree dirty.
#
# The rest matches what `horus new --cpp` generates, so `horus new my_robot
# --from differential_drive_cpp` hands you the same .gitignore the blank C++
# template would have.

# HORUS environment (auto-managed by `horus run`)
.horus/packages/
.horus/bin/
.horus/lib/
.horus/include/
.horus/cache/
.horus/target/
.horus/Cargo.toml
.horus/Cargo.lock
*.log

# C++
build/
.horus/cpp-build/
compile_commands.json
*.o
*.so
*.a
